<title>UK: NWE jet fuel firm, high prices discourage buyers.</title>
<headline>NWE jet fuel firm, high prices discourage buyers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fuel prices were steady on Tuesday but traders said recent high premiums were scaring off buyers.</p>
<p>On the cif cargo market premiums were assessed at Sept IPE +$30/+32, cif NWE per tonne.</p>
<p>&quot;Buyers seem to be keeping out while these levels persist,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Availability in the Mediterranean was still tight. Premiums on a Libyan cargo were put at quotes fob Med +$9/$10.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
</text>
